From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix AN7563 RX skb alignment

AN7563 reserves NET_SKB_PAD plus NET_IP_ALIGN bytes before the RX packet
so that QDMA's two-byte offset mode can place the Ethernet header at the
expected address.  The queue entry points at that packet address, not at
the beginning of the page-pool fragment.

Passing the packet address to napi_build_skb() shifts skb_shared_info by
34 bytes.  Its dataref field is consequently only two-byte aligned on
32-bit ARM and skb_clone() raises an alignment exception as soon as a
received packet is cloned.

Build the skb from the original fragment address and reserve the AN7563
headroom afterwards, matching the page-pool RX layout used by the Airoha
driver before the unified EN7523 changes.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2364,10 +2364,16 @@ static struct sk_buff *airoha_qdma_build_rx_skb(struct airoha_queue *q,
 		u32 desc_ctrl = le32_to_cpu(READ_ONCE(desc->ctrl));
 		u32 len = FIELD_GET(QDMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, desc_ctrl);
 
-		skb = napi_build_skb(e->buf, q->buf_size);
+		if (airoha_is(q->qdma->eth, airoha_an7563))
+			skb = napi_build_skb(e->buf - AIROHA_AN7563_RX_HEADROOM,
+					     q->buf_size);
+		else
+			skb = napi_build_skb(e->buf, q->buf_size);
 		if (!skb)
 			return NULL;
 
+		if (airoha_is(q->qdma->eth, airoha_an7563))
+			skb_reserve(skb, AIROHA_AN7563_RX_HEADROOM);
 		__skb_put(skb, len);
 		if ((netdev->features & NETIF_F_RXCSUM) &&
 		    airoha_qdma_rx_checksum_ok(q->qdma->eth, desc))
-- 
2.51.0
